ns to Protect State Ratepayers Take Center Stage","src":"The Capitol Forum","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","date":"2026-11-17","zh":""},{"title":"NextEra Energy Turned $1,000 Into More Than $3,000 Over a Decade, but Only Into About $1,100 Over the Past Five Years","src":"24/7 Wall St.","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","date":"2026-11-17","zh":"NextEra Energy 在十年內將 1,000 美元變成了 3,000 多美元，但在過去五年中只變成了 1,100 美元左右"}],"themes":[{"name":"能源/電力","count":10},{"name":"訂單/合約","count":6},{"name":"併購","count":6},{"name":"加密貨幣","count":1},{"name":"財報","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-13","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/753308/000075330826000015/nee-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"NEE is one of the largest electric power and energy infrastructure companies in North America. As of December 31, 2025, NEE had approximately 80 gigawatts of net generation and storage capacity from a diverse portfolio of assets, primarily including natural gas, wind, solar and nuclear generation facilities and battery storage facilities. NEE has two principal businesses, FPL and NEER. FPL is the largest electric utility in Florida and the U.S. FPL's strategic focus is centered on investing in generation, storage, transmission and distribution facilities to deliver on its value proposition of keeping customer bills low and delivering high reliability, outstanding customer service and energy from diverse generation sources for the benefit of its more than six million customer accounts. NEER is one of the largest energy infrastructure developers in the U.S. NEER's strategic focus is center","zh":"NEE是北美最大的電力和能源基礎設施公司之一。截至2025年12月31日，NEE擁有約80吉瓦的淨發電和儲存容量，來自多元化的資產組合，主要包括天然氣、風能、太陽能和核能發電設施以及電池儲存設施。 NEE有兩個主要業務：FPL和NEER。 FPL 是佛羅裡達州和美國最大的電力公司。 FPL 的策略重點是投資發電、儲存、輸電和配電設施，以實現其價值主張，即保持低客戶帳單並提供高可靠性、出色的客戶服務和來自不同發電來源的能源，以造福於其超過 600 萬客戶帳戶。 NEER是美國最大的能源基礎設施開發商之一 NEER的戰略重點是中心"},{"en":"NEE seeks to create value in its two principal businesses by meeting customer needs more economically and reliably than its competitors. NEE's strategy has resulted in profitable growth over sustained periods at both FPL and NEER. Management seeks to grow each business (see Note 15 – Commitments) in a manner consistent with the varying opportunities available to it; however, management believes that the diversification and balance represented by FPL and NEER is a valuable characteristic of the enterprise and recognizes that each business contributes to NEE's financial strength in different ways. FPL and NEER share a common platform with the objective of lowering costs, creating efficiencies and encouraging innovative ideas for their businesses. NEE and its subsidiaries, with employees totaling approximately 17,400 as of December 31, 2025, continue to develop and implement enterprise-wide","zh":"NEE 尋求比競爭對手更經濟、更可靠地滿足客戶需求，從而在兩大主要業務中創造價值。 NEE 的策略導致 FPL 和 NEER 的獲利持續成長。管理層力求以與其可獲得的不同機會相一致的方式發展每項業務（參見附註 15 – 承諾）；然而，管理層認為，以FPL和NEER為代表的多元化和平衡性是企業的一個寶貴特徵，並認識到每項業務以不同的方式為NEE的財務實力做出貢獻。 FPL 和 NEER 共享一個共同平台，旨在降低成本、提高效率並鼓勵業務創新。截至 2025 年 12 月 31 日，NEE 及其子公司的員工總數約為 17,400 人，繼續在企業範圍內開發和實施"},{"en":"NEE's reportable segments for financial reporting purposes are FPL and NEER (see Note 16). NEECH, a wholly owned subsidiary of NEE, owns and provides funding for NEE's operating subsidiaries, other than FPL and its subsidiaries. The following diagram depicts NEE's simplified ownership structure:","zh":"為財務報告目的，NEE 的可報告分部為 FPL 和 NEER（請參閱附註 16）。 NEECH 是 NEE 的全資子公司，擁有 NEE 的營運子公司（FPL 及其子公司除外）並為其提供資金。下圖描述了NEE的簡化所有權結構："}],"markets":[{"en":"Electricity markets in the U.S. and Canada are regional and diverse in character. All are extensively regulated, and competition in these markets is shaped and constrained by regulation. The nature of the products offered varies based on the specifics of regulation in each region. Generally, in addition to the natural constraints on pricing freedom presented by competition, NEER may also face specific constraints in the form of price caps, or maximum allowed prices, for certain products. NEER's ability to sell the output of its generation facilities may also be constrained by available transmission capacity, which can vary from time to time and can have a significant impact on pricing.","zh":"美國和加拿大的電力市場具有區域性和多樣性。所有這些都受到廣泛的監管，這些市場的競爭受到監管的影響和限制。所提供產品的性質根據每個地區的監管具體情況而有所不同。一般來說，除了競爭帶來的定價自由的自然限制外，NEER 還可能面臨某些產品的價格上限或最高允許價格形式的具體限制。 NEER 出售其發電設施產出的能力也可能受到可用傳輸容量的限制，可用傳輸容量可能會不時變化，並對定價產生重大影響。"},{"en":"The degree and nature of competition is different in wholesale markets than in retail markets. A majority of NEER's revenues are derived from sales of energy, capacity, credits and ancillary products under long-term PPAs to customers located in wholesale electricity markets. Wholesale power generation is a capital-intensive, commodity-driven business with numerous industry participants. NEER primarily competes on the basis of price, but believes that its track record of completing projects on schedule, creditworthiness, operating scale and ability to offer and manage reliable customized risk solutions to wholesale customers are competitive advantages. Wholesale power generation is a regional business that is highly fragmented relative to many other commodity industries and diverse in terms of industry structure. As such, there is a wide variation in terms of the capabilities, resources, ","zh":"批發市場的競爭程度和性質與零售市場不同。 NEER 的大部分收入來自根據長期購電協議向批發電力市場的客戶銷售能源、容量、信貸和輔助產品。批發發電是一項資本密集、商品驅動型業務，產業參與者眾多。 NEER 主要在價格上競爭，但相信其按期完成專案的記錄、信譽、營運規模以及為批發客戶提供和管理可靠的客製化風險解決方案的能力都是競爭優勢。批發發電是一項區域性業務，與許多其他大宗商品行業相比，其高度分散且行業結構多樣化。因此，在能力、資源、"}],"customers":[{"en":"FPL's primary source of operating revenues is from its retail customer base; it also serves a limited number of wholesale customers within Florida. The percentage of FPL's operating revenues and customer accounts by customer class were as follows:","zh":"FPL 的主要營業收入來源是其零售客戶群；它還為佛羅裡達州內數量有限的批發客戶提供服務。依客戶類別劃分的 FPL 營業收入和客戶帳戶百分比如下："},{"en":"For both retail and wholesale customers, the prices (or rates) that FPL may charge are approved by regulatory bodies, by the FPSC in the case of retail customers and by the FERC in the case of wholesale customers. In general, under U.S. and Florida law, regulated rates are intended to cover the cost of providing service, including a reasonable rate of return on invested capital. Since the regulatory bodies have authority to determine the relevant cost of providing service and the appropriate rate of return on capital employed, there can be no guarantee that FPL will be able to earn any particular rate of return or recover all of its costs through regulated rates. See FPL Regulation below.","zh":"对于零售和批发客户，FPL 可能收取的价格（或费率）由监管机构批准，对于零售客户则由 FPSC 批准，对于批发客户则由 FERC 批准。一般来说，根据美国和佛罗里达州的法律，监管费率旨在涵盖提供服务的成本，包括合理的投资资本回报率。由于监管机构有权确定提供服务的相关成本以及所用资本的适当回报率，因此无法保证 FPL 能够获得任何特定回报率或通过监管利率收回所有成本。請參閱下面的 FPL 法規。"}],"competition":[],"segments":{},"peers":["D","DUK","SO","ABBV","AEP"]}}